('CWLR 221F', 'CWLR', '221F', 'LOW RESIDENCY CROSS-GENRE WORKSHOP', 'Humanities, Arts, and Soc Sci', 'Creative Writing', 2, 4, '2 to 4 Units, Workshop, 10 to 20 hours per quarter; activity, 3 to 6 hours. Prerequisite(s): graduate standing. Focuses on the production of original work. Includes introductory study of chosen cross-genres. Emphasizes technique, structure, style, and form. F. Fiction; N. Nonfiction; P. Poetry; S. Screenwriting; T. Playwriting. Each segment is repeatable.'),
